---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Privacy | DanielNG">
<div class="container">
  <div class="row">
    <div class="col-md-auto pageTitle">
      privacy
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="row justify-content-center">
    <div class="col-md-8 privacyText">
      <p>This site doesn't use cookies, doesn't store anything on your device, and doesn't sell or share your data with anyone.</p>

      <h2>What gets collected</h2>
      <p>When you view a page, your browser sends a small request back to this site that records:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>the page you're on and the site or campaign link that brought you here</li>
        <li>your screen and window width (rounded to the nearest 100px), language, time zone and light/dark mode</li>
        <li>roughly how long the page was open and how far you scrolled</li>
        <li>which links off the site you click, like LinkedIn or the resume download</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Like every website, the hosting provider (Amazon CloudFront) also logs each request with your IP address and browser details.</p>

      <h2>Why</h2>
      <p>To see how many people visit, where they come from and which pages they read. It's used only by me, only in aggregate, and never to identify you or follow you to other sites. Visits are grouped by day, and there's no way to recognize you on a later visit.</p>

      <h2>Opting out</h2>
      <p>If your browser sends Global Privacy Control or Do Not Track, the page-view request isn't sent at all.</p>

      <h2>How long it's kept</h2>
      <p>The logs are deleted automatically after 90 days.</p>

      <h2>Questions or requests</h2>
      <p>To ask what's held about you or to have it deleted, message me on <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/ngardnerdaniel/" class="linkstyling">LinkedIn</a> or on Instagram at @danielng.exe.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
</BaseLayout>
